facts:
A square of area $A$ has side length $\sqrt{A}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3,3);
\node at (1.5,1.5) {$A$};
\node[below] at (1.5,0) {$\sqrt{A}$};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$\sqrt{A}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
Find the side length of this square.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.0,3.0);
\node at (1.5,1.5) {$36\text{ cm}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
$\sqrt{36}$
$=6$
The side length is $6$ cm.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.0,3.0);
\node at (1.5,1.5) {$36\text{ cm}^{2}$};
\node[below] at (1.5,0) {$6\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

